Spec: TemplateSystem

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Run `agent template system`: the offline, Helm-less templating leaf for the system
    kind. It turns the parsed flags plus an on-disk package tree into a complete system
    context without any cluster contact, renders the package CRDs and `systems` manifests
    through Handlebars scripts, and prints the result to stdout as multi-document YAML.
    Dispatched by @Commands::System in ./mod.rs — the one template leaf whose failure
    lane exits 3. Its @Parameters is narrower than the tenant/service twins: no
    `--template-dir`, no `--agent-image`.

Depends on:
  ./mod.sdd — owns the embedded @Contexts enum, the @Commands::System wiring, and the
    leaf-@Err lane (`Templating a system package failed with: {e:}` then
    @std::process::exit(3) — the only template leaf not exiting 1).
  ./tenant.sdd, ./service.sdd — reviewed sibling specs of the tenant/service leaves. The
    Rust source here is tenant.rs modulo a real two-hunk diff: the @Parameters field
    `template_dir` (`-t`/`--template-dir`, env `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, default
    `./agent/templates`) and the field `agent_image` (`--agent-image`, env
    `AGENT_IMAGE`, default @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE) are dropped, and the third
    resolver segment `{}/tenant` becomes `{}/system`. The derives, the remaining nine
    flag definitions, the embedded snippet text and the evaluation order are
    byte-shared; every other behavioural drift is script-side — this lane runs only the
    `crds`/`systems` categories, ships an identity kind default instead of a hardcoded
    overlay block, and its script `context.rhai` omits the twins' `template_dir`/
    `agent_image` context overlay.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new assembly and resolver-order semantics, the
    @Script::eval @crate::Result conversion, the Deref'd @Script::set_dynamic, and the
    behaviour of the script-level `import_run` / `import_template` helpers: missing
    module skips with the unit, a present module without a `template` function falls
    back to its `run`, and both missing skips. Engine contents are attributed to that
    build and `vynil-core` `0.7.7`. The fallback is what makes the shipped
    `context_system` (which defines only `run`) an identity in the template lane.
  /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd — the `new_hbs` / `register_partial_dir` /
    `register_helper_dir` / `render_named` script surface the render phase uses; render
    semantics (strict mode, no-escape, same-name re-registration overwrite) are that
    spec's contract, not restated here.
  /common/src/context.sdd — documents that @common::context::init_k8s is not called by
    this dispatcher or leaf; this file reaches nothing in the crate context module.
  /common/src/instancesystem.sdd, /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @system_rhai_register
    and @package_rhai_register are installed by the chosen @Script::new engine but the
    frozen render path never names them; the engine choice (full @Script::new, not
    @Script::new_core) is what this reference freezes.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Result and @common::Error::SerializationError;
    @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE is no longer referenced here because the same diff hunk
    that drops `--agent-image` removes this leaf's only Rust-side use of it.
  /agent/scripts/system/context.rhai, /agent/scripts/system/context_system.rhai,
    /agent/scripts/system/template.rhai, /agent/scripts/system/template_crds.rhai,
    /agent/scripts/system/template_systems.rhai — the system modules the embedded
    snippet imports and the per-category emitters they run; unspecified so far (open
    task in /agent/agent.sdd), so this spec freezes the behaviour the leaf depends on.
    `context_system` ships only a `run` identity and reaches this lane via the
    run-fallback; it is the kind-default slot a package shadows.
  /agent/scripts/lib/build_context.rhai, /agent/scripts/lib/install_from_dir.rhai,
    /agent/scripts/lib/storage_class_enrich.rhai — shared machinery the system modules
    invoke transitively (context assembly, bucketed category rendering and stdout
    emission, storage-class enrichment — a pure static table with no host or cluster
    calls). `build_context::template` never reads `template_dir`/`agent_image`, so the
    dropped keys cannot leak into context assembly.
  Workspace @clap (argument parsing), @serde/@serde_json (@Parameters serde derives and
    the args JSON), @std::path::PathBuf.

Exposes:
  @Parameters — `#[derive(@clap::Args, @std::fmt::Debug, serde @Serialize, @Deserialize)]
    pub struct @Parameters` with exactly the nine private fields listed in Accepts, one
    fewer pair than the twins; embedded as @Commands::System in ./mod.rs and serialized
    into the script's `args` dynamic under the Rust field names.
  @run — `pub fn @run(@args: &@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>`: synchronous, called
    un-awaited from ./mod.rs; no `@must_use`; the whole contract of the leaf.

Accepts:
  Nine optional arguments, each with an env fallback and a default; the leaf runs with
    zero CLI arguments, and relative defaults resolve against the process working
    directory.
  `--namespace` / `-n`, env `NAMESPACE`, value name `NAMESPACE`, default `default` —
    @Parameters.namespace, the instance namespace.
  `--instance` / `-i`, env `INSTANCE`, value name `INSTANCE`, default `instance-name` —
    @Parameters.instance, the instance name.
  `--vynil-namespace` / `-v`, env `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, value name `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`,
    default `vynil-system` — @Parameters.vynil_namespace.
  `--source` / `-o`, env `SOURCE`, value name `SOURCE`, default `/src` —
    @Parameters.package_dir, the package tree root (Chart-less layout, see Must).
  `--script-dir` / `-s`, env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value name `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, default
    `./agent/scripts` — @Parameters.script_dir, the shipped agent Rhai tree root.
  `--tag`, env `TAG`, value name `TAG`, default `1.0.0` — @Parameters.tag, the requested
    version (no short flag).
  `--config-dir` / `-c`, env `CONFIG_DIR`, value name `CONFIG_DIR`, default `.` —
    @Parameters.config_dir, also a Handlebars partial dir and a resolver dir.
  `--controller-values`, env `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, value name `CONTROLLER_VALUES`,
    default `{}` — @Parameters.controller_values, raw JSON text, never parsed on the
    Rust side.
  `--context`, env `CONTEXT_NAME`, value name `CONTEXT_NAME`, `value_enum` over
    ./mod.sdd's @Contexts, `default_value_t` → @Contexts::@Simple — offline
    cluster-profile selector.
  The twins' `--template-dir` / `-t` / `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY` and `--agent-image` /
    `AGENT_IMAGE` do not exist on this leaf: passing either flag is an @clap unknown-
    argument parse failure, and those two env variables are never consulted.
  Package tree read by the frozen path — `${package_dir}/package.yaml` mandatory (raw
    read); optional `${package_dir}/handlebars/partials/` and
    `${package_dir}/handlebars/helpers/`; only two category dirs are ever probed —
    `crds` and `systems` — containing multi-doc `.yaml`/`.yml` and their
    `.yaml.hbs`/`.yml.hbs` template counterparts; the tenant/service dirs befores,
    vitals, others, scalables and posts are never probed here even when present.
  Hook modules resolved by name — context_pre, context_extra, context_post, install_pre,
    install_crds_pre, install_crds_post, install_systems_pre are package- or
    config-provided only; context_system ships as the resolver fallback; the
    naming-convention slot install_systems_post is never resolved by the shipped
    emitter (Tasks). Optional cluster file `${config_dir}/agent.yaml`.

Returns:
  @Ok(`()`) when the single embedded snippet completes; the script's final value is
    discarded (`let _ = @Script::eval(…)?`), and success falls off ./mod.rs to exit 0.
  During the run — rendered manifests on process stdout, one `---` line then one
    `yaml_encode` document per object, in the fixed crds-then-systems order and bucket
    order of Must; the CRD pass additionally prints a separator without a following
    document for every ignored non-CRD item (Must, Tasks). Logs go through @tracing and
    the script console helpers, stdout through the engine print hook (both attributed to
    the core build).
  Nothing is written to disk by this lane — file-collision and overwrite policy belong
    to the install lanes, not here.

Raises:
  @common::Error::SerializationError (display `SerializationError: {0}`) if
    @serde_json::to_value(@Parameters) fails — see Tasks, that serialization is total
    today.
  @common::Error::Core wrapping the core Rhai failure (text `Rhai script error: <rhai
    text>`, conversion owned by /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd) for snippet parse errors,
    failure to resolve the `context` or `template` modules from the resolver path, an
    unreadable or unparsable `package.yaml`, a Handlebars render or YAML parse failure
    rethrown by the render phase, or any script `throw`.
  The leaf catches nothing itself — ./mod.rs turns every @Err into the frozen system log
    line and @std::process::exit(3).

Handles:
  Invalid `--controller-values` JSON — the script catches, console-warns, and renders
    with `controller` as the empty `#{}` map; the run continues.
  Missing optional inputs (no `agent.yaml`, absent `crds` or `systems` dir, absent
    hooks) — empty-default branches, no error; with neither category dir present the
    run succeeds emitting nothing on stdout.
  Hook returning a non-map (including the missing-module skip unit) — context kept
    unchanged, except the `context_extra` result which is assigned unguarded, so a plain
    default run carries `extra` as the skip unit (Tasks).
  The shipped `context_system` default — no `template` function, so the fallback calls
    its identity `run` and the context passes through unchanged.
  `crds` documents whose `kind` is not `CustomResourceDefinition` — separator printed,
    document skipped, `# Ignoring an item as it is not a CRD` console-warned (Tasks).
  `systems` documents that are not maps or lack `kind`/a map `metadata` — console-warned
    and excluded by the shared bucketed pass.
  No arguments at all — every default applies; the run then fails only because
    `/src/package.yaml` is normally absent.

Must:
  Build the engine as exactly @Script::new(vec![`${package_dir}/scripts`,
    `${config_dir}`, `${script_dir}/system`, `${script_dir}/lib`]) in that order, so
    package scripts first, the config dir, the system category dir and the shared lib
    dir resolve imports first-provider-wins — a package's `scripts/context.rhai` or
    `scripts/template.rhai` therefore shadows the shipped system modules.
  Inject `args` once via the Deref'd @Script::set_dynamic from the
    @serde_json::to_value(@Parameters) JSON — exactly nine keys (the Rust field names),
    paths are display strings, @Contexts as `"Simple"`/`"HA"` — the only way
    @Parameters reaches the scripts; there is no `template_dir` and no `agent_image`
    key, and the shipped context builder adds no lane-level overlay for them either, so
    render data never carries those two names (Tasks).
  Execute exactly the embedded snippet sequence, byte-shared with the twins:
    `import("context")` as ctx; build the `instance` map as `#{ metadata: #{ name:
    args.instance, namespace: args.namespace } }`; `ctx::template(instance, args)`;
    `import("template")`; `template::run(instance, context)`.
  Stay cluster-free on the frozen path. The `instance` is synthesized from the two
    flags only — no CR is ever fetched and no @kube::Client is built by any layer of the
    fixed flow, which is why the missing @common::context::init_k8s and missing async
    runtime upstream cost nothing here.
  Read exactly these disk inputs — `${package_dir}/package.yaml` (mandatory),
    `${config_dir}/agent.yaml` (optional), `is_dir` probes of `crds` and `systems`, and
    every file inside the present category dirs.
  Assemble the context in this order (shared /agent/scripts/lib/build_context.rhai
    `template` plus /agent/scripts/system/context.rhai): decode `package.yaml`; parse
    `--controller-values` into `controller` (or `#{}` plus warn); build `cluster` from
    `agent.yaml` or `#{}` then force `storage_classes` (enriched enum-default storage
    classes), `crds` (enum-default list), `services` `[]`, and `vynil_namespace` from
    the flag (overriding `agent.yaml`), with `prefered_storage` and `ha` set only when
    `agent.yaml` omits them; take the cluster node/CRD/storage-class defaults from the
    `--context` enum (`@Contexts::@HA` selects the eight-node/~160-CRD/three-storage-class
    hardcoded profile, anything else the single-node/empty-CRD/one-storage-class profile,
    matched as the string `args.context_name == "HA"`); set `defaults` to each
    `package.yaml` option's `default` member and `values` equal to `defaults` (plain
    equality — instance-side options cannot participate because the synthesized instance
    has no `spec`); build `instance` with the package metadata block (`jukebox` hardcoded
    `box`, `images` and `resources` passed through), labels/selector emitting
    `app.kubernetes.io/...` plus `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-namespace`,
    `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-category` from the package category and literal
    `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-type` `system` (on this lane the literal matches the kind),
    `appslug`, `current` `""` and `requested` from `--tag`; then the hook chain
    `context_pre`, `context_system`, `context_extra`, `context_post` in exactly that
    order — pre/system/post guarded to replace the context only when a map comes back
    (the shipped `context_system` passes through the run-fallback identity), while
    `context_extra` lands in `extra` unguarded. No hardcoded kind block is inserted —
    unlike the tenant lane's `tenant` block and the service lane's `namespace` block,
    this lane overlays nothing of its own — and the template chain stops at
    `context_post`; `context_after` exists only in the context module's install-lane
    `run`.
  Render and emit in this fixed order (/agent/scripts/system/template.rhai):
    `install_pre` guarded hook, then `is_dir` probe of `${package_dir}/crds` →
    `import_run("template_crds")` with the map-guarded context return, then `is_dir`
    probe of `${package_dir}/systems` → `import_run("template_systems")`, likewise
    guarded — the only two categories, and the emitters resolve through `run` where the
    context-stage hooks resolve through `template`-with-fallback.
  Run the CRD emitter (shipped /agent/scripts/system/template_crds.rhai) as:
    `install_crds_pre` guarded hook; fresh Handlebars engine per call (partials from
    `${config_dir}` and `${package_dir}/handlebars/partials`, helpers from
    `${package_dir}/handlebars/helpers`, strict mode); read every file in
    `${package_dir}/crds`, decoding `.yaml`/`.yml` directly and rendering
    `.yaml.hbs`/`.yml.hbs` through `render_named` per file with the whole context as
    data; for each decoded document check `kind` — a `CustomResourceDefinition` prints
    `---` then `yaml_encode`, any other value prints `---`, console-warns `# Ignoring an
    item as it is not a CRD` and emits no document (Tasks); `install_crds_post` guarded
    hook; return the context.
  Run the systems emitter as: `install_systems_pre` guarded hook, one shared bucketed
    pass (/agent/scripts/lib/install_from_dir.rhai `template`) over
    `${package_dir}/systems` that builds its own fresh Handlebars engine, decodes and
    renders the same two file-suffix pairs, drops shape-invalid documents with a
    console warning and prints `---` plus `yaml_encode` bucket-ordered by the shared
    first/middle/last kind lists (their contents owned by that file); it never resolves
    an `install_systems_post` (Tasks); return the context.
  Keep the emission unsorted at every stage — kind-bucket order, then source-file
    iteration within a bucket — so byte-identical reruns ride on directory-iteration
    order (Tasks).

Must not:
  Read a kubeconfig, construct a @kube::Client, or touch `vynil-core` cluster state on
    the frozen path — the leaf's offline claim breaks the moment a fixed step calls a
    registered cluster name, and the shipped system template modules never do; only the
    install-lane `run` bodies in that same script dir reach the cluster.
  Render the package through @read_package_yaml or the @VynilPackageSource model — the
    template lane reads `package.yaml` as raw YAML (the validating reader belongs to the
    install lane), so `agent template system` accepts documents the model would reject.
  Write rendered output to files — stdout is the only output channel, so no collision or
    overwrite decision exists to reinstate here.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the scenarios — the file has no @tests module and /agent/tests only matches
      the word `template` inside unrelated Rhai lib/lifecycle fixtures. Name tests after
      the scenarios and freeze the nine-key args-JSON set plus the @Contexts wire
      strings once.
  [?] Cross-ref ./tenant.sdd Tasks — as the Rust files differ by only two hunks, these
      open tenant decisions bind this leaf verbatim: the unreachable
      @map_err(@common::Error::SerializationError) arm, the unguarded `context["extra"]`
      assignment (same shape in /agent/scripts/system/context.rhai), the no-sort plus
      plain `yaml_encode` determinism question (the ordered variant's guarantees are
      /common/src/yamlhandler.sdd's), the `1.0.0`/`instance-name` placeholder defaults
      (the @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE half has no twin here because this leaf dropped
      it), the shared @Script::new host powers on an offline lane, and the three-leaf
      @Parameters unification — this leaf is the hunk that broke the byte-identical
      twin story.
  [?] Dropped-keys consequence — `args` carries no `template_dir`/`agent_image` keys and
      /agent/scripts/system/context.rhai also omits the twins' `context["template_dir"]`
      / `context["agent_image"]` overlay, so a system render can never see an agent
      image or template directory. The shipped system modules never reach for those
      names, but a hook, partial or Handlebars template ported from the tenant/service
      data contract reads a missing-map-property/unit instead of a path string and
      strict renders on such references fail at render time. Decide whether the lane is
      deliberately keyless (and document it for package authors) or the keys return —
      the unification decision above may settle it.
  [?] Kind-default identity slot — the shipped `context_system.rhai` completes nothing
      (contrast `context_service`'s block-completing `template`), so it exists only as a
      shadowable no-op reached via the run-fallback. Decide whether system packages are
      expected to carry their own kind block in a shadow and whether the identity stub
      should stay, be deleted (module-not-found skips identically), or gain a real
      default.
  [?] /agent/scripts/system/template_crds.rhai prints the `---` separator before
      checking `kind`, so every ignored non-CRD document leaves an unmatched separator
      on stdout — an empty document between separators in the stream (stream consumers
      may reject or silently skip it) while the warning goes to the log channel. Decide
      whether the filter should run before the separator.
  [?] `install_systems_post` is a dead hook slot — /agent/scripts/system/template_systems.rhai
      resolves only `install_systems_pre` around the shared pass, mirroring the
      tenant/service lanes where bucketed `scalables` likewise has no post hook while its
      bespoke categories have both; here `crds` (bespoke) carries pre and post and
      `systems` (bucketed) carries only pre. Resolve together with the script-side half
      of ./tenant.sdd's twin-drift entry.

Done when:
  Every scenario has a passing mapped test, the nine-key args-JSON shape and resolver
    shadow order are pinned, and the three-leaf duplication carries either a unification
    or a per-leaf written justification.

Scenario: Offline render of a full system package tree
  Given a package dir with `package.yaml`, populated `crds` and `systems` dirs of
    `.yaml.hbs` files and an unreachable cluster
  When @run executes the frozen path
  Then context assembly reads only disk inputs and no registration of the k8s surface is
    ever called
  And stdout carries `---` plus one YAML document per object — CRDs in file iteration
    order first, then the `systems` documents in first/middle/last kind order
  And @run returns @Ok
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Shipped kind default passes the context through
  Given a package tree with no hook modules anywhere
  When @run assembles the context
  Then `context_system` resolves through the `import_template` run-fallback and returns
    the context unchanged
  And the context carries the shared build plus an unguarded `extra` holding the
    `context_extra` skip unit, and no `tenant`/`namespace`-style kind block exists
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Category dirs absent yields empty stdout
  Given a package tree with only `package.yaml` and neither `crds` nor `systems`
  When @run executes
  Then both dirs are probed with `is_dir` and skipped without error
  And stdout is empty and @run returns @Ok, reaching exit 0 through ./mod.rs
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Non-CRD document is ignored but leaves its separator
  Given `${package_dir}/crds` holding one file with a `CustomResourceDefinition` and a
    `ConfigMap` document
  When the CRD emitter classifies the decoded documents
  Then the CRD prints as `---` plus its encoding
  And the `ConfigMap` prints only a further `---` line, console-warns `# Ignoring an
    item as it is not a CRD`, and contributes no document — stdout carries an empty
    stream document at that position (Tasks)
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Systems pass emits bucketed and skips its post slot
  Given a package whose `scripts/install_systems_post.rhai` returns a context plus a
    `from_post` marker
  When the systems category runs
  Then the post hook is never imported and `from_post` never reaches the render data
  And the shared bucketed pass still prints every valid `systems` document after the
    first/middle/last kind lists
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Invalid controller values continue with empty controller
  Given `--controller-values not-json`
  When context assembly parses it
  Then the script catch console-warns and `controller` stays `#{}`
  And rendering completes and @run returns @Ok
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Context enum selects the offline cluster profile
  Given the same package tree rendered twice, once with `--context HA` and once with the
    @Contexts::@Simple default
  When both runs finish
  Then the HA run carries the eight-node profile, a non-empty default `crds` list and
    three enriched storage classes
  And the Simple run carries `nodes` `["single"]`, empty `crds` and one `local-path`
    storage class
  And `cluster.ha` is `true` for HA and `false` for Simple unless `agent.yaml` overrides
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Package scripts shadow the shipped system modules
  Given `${package_dir}/scripts/template.rhai` defining `run` differs from
    /agent/scripts/system/template.rhai
  When @run imports `template`
  Then the package copy resolves first per the resolver order and its emit set runs
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Unreadable package fails through the system exit lane
  Given `--source` pointing at a directory with no `package.yaml`
  When context assembly reads it
  Then the script failure propagates as @common::Error::Core (`Rhai script error: …`)
  And ./mod.rs logs `Templating a system package failed with: {e:}` and exits 3 — not 1
    like the tenant/service twins
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  `args` as the scripts see it with all defaults: `namespace` `default`, `instance`
    `instance-name`, `vynil_namespace` `vynil-system`, `package_dir` `/src`,
    `script_dir` `./agent/scripts`, `tag` `1.0.0`, `config_dir` `.`,
    `controller_values` `{}`, `context_name` `Simple` — nine keys, no `template_dir`,
    no `agent_image`.
  stdout frame: `---` line, then one YAML document, per object; one unmatched `---` with
    no document per ignored non-CRD item; no closing separator.
